# Exercise the actual website link dispatcher, including the formerly missing action.
import ../../site/actions.dl
import site_fixture.dl

the site's pages means: [home page, IDE page]

set painter to (the function named "paint the website Farm $") as a pointer
require condition (painter != (0 as a pointer)) reporting "The Farm surface has no painter"
set instance to an instance of website fixture
set driver to a website shader test driver
set view to a new UI view
set view's driver to the address of driver
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set state's route to "/index.html"
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
initialize the website Farm in (the address of state)
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Open the farm challenge →" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the value of "Challenge views" in (the address of instance)) = 2) reporting "The production Farm link did not select the declarative challenge"
set document to state's farm's document
require condition ((document != (0 as a pointer to website farm document)) and (document's selected = "worker-1")) reporting "Opening Farm did not initialize its live document"
require condition (state's farm's graphics phase = 1) reporting "Opening Farm did not request the actual DynLex scene graph"
set editor to the UI source editor labeled "Farm source" in (state's language)
require condition ((the UI main source of editor in (state's language) at 0.0 seconds) = (the string form of (the website farm lumberjack source))) reporting "The Farm editor must load the selected role through the shared source workspace"
set flags to the length of document's world's flags
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Add flag" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the length of document's world's flags) = flags + 1) reporting "The Add flag action did not update the live world"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Remove flag" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the length of document's world's flags) = flags) reporting "The Remove flag action did not update the live world"
set the text of "Farm area name" in (the address of instance) to "Vegetable patch"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Draw area" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
finish website Farm area from (website farm point 3 3) to (website farm point 5 4) in (the address of state)
require condition ((the length of document's world's areas) = 1) reporting "The work-area controls did not retain their drawn rectangle"
set the text of "Farm area name" in (the address of instance) to "My field"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Rename area" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the item at 0 in (document's world's areas))'s name = "My field") reporting "The work-area rename control did not change its model"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Delete area" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the length of document's world's areas) = 0) reporting "The work-area delete control did not remove its model"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "One turn" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition (document's world's tick = 1) reporting "The Farm turn control did not advance the simulation"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Start farm ▶" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition (state's farm's playing) reporting "The Farm play control did not start playback"
set the text of "Farm area name" in (the address of instance) to "Unfinished field"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Draw area" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition (state's farm's drawing = 1) reporting "The unfinished area test did not enter drawing mode"
set instance's event target to the control labeled "Reset farm" in (the address of instance)
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((state's farm's document's world's tick = 0) and (state's farm's playing = false)) reporting "Reset did not replace the live world and stop playback"
require condition ((state's farm's drawing = 0) and (state's farm's drawing name is empty)) reporting "Reset retained the unfinished area from the previous world"
set instance's event target to the UI element labeled "← Choose a challenge" in farm challenge
follow website link (the address of instance)
require condition ((the value of "Challenge views" in (the address of instance)) = 0) reporting "Returning to the gallery did not leave the Farm view"
close website Farm in (the address of state)
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != (0 as a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close the address of instance
print line "The production Farm link opens its declarative UI, loads the shared editor, advances, plays, resets and returns to the gallery."
